static lstr L3003 = {0, 5, "E0530"};
static lstr L3004 = {0, 419, "Shape converts a type to and from a Value tree. The compiler provides it for bool, int, f64, char, string, Array<T>, Map<string, V>, Option<T> and tuples of two to four items whose contents implement it. A struct or enum needs an `implement Shape` block. A Map with keys other than string, a function and a sized integer have no Value form.\012Fix: use a Map<string, V>, or wrap the type in a struct that implements Shape."};
static lstr L3005 = {0, 5, "E0531"};
